# Testing Rules

- Framework: Vitest
- Every pure function in `src/policy/` and `src/risk/` must have unit tests
- Cover both happy path and edge cases

## Required Edge Cases (must be tested)

- Zero / dust amounts
- Exactly at limit boundaries (maxPositionSize, maxDailyLoss, maxConcentration)
- Assets not in allowlist
- Futures when only SPOT is allowed
- Missing or stale market data
- Concurrent / rapid proposals
- Malformed proposals
- Empty mandate / missing required fields
- Extreme volatility spikes
- Partial fill scenarios (when relevant)

## Test Structure

- Use `describe` / `it` blocks
- Prefer table-driven tests for rule permutations
- Mock MCP client in integration tests
- Demo Mode and Live Mode should share the same core test suite where possible

## Coverage Expectation

Aim for high coverage on policy and risk modules. Core decision path must be fully covered.
